# The libraries Patina needs on Windows, pinned by digest: GitHub release
# assets are not immutable. Read by packaging/windows-deps.ps1, which ci.yml
# and release.yml run; the workflows also load these lines into their env.
#
# libmpv: mpv's own LGPL build of libmpv for Windows, built by mpv's CI
# from the release's signed tag (ci/build-mingw64-full.sh) and attached to
# the release, which keeps it; the one Patina's Windows folder carries,
# with the LICENSE.LGPL beside it. Its libmpv-2.dll needs only Windows' own
# DLLs: it loads Vulkan's only when asked for Vulkan, which Patina never
# does. mpv publishes these since 0.42.0. The release is not immutable
# (mpv's publish script re-uploads with --clobber), so the digest is the pin.
# To bump, at a new mpv release, take the asset's URL and digest:
#   gh api repos/mpv-player/mpv/releases/latest --jq '.assets[] | select(.name | test("^libmpv-v.*-x86_64-w64-mingw32-lgpl\\.zip$")) | "\(.browser_download_url) \(.digest | ltrimstr("sha256:"))"'
# and check its signature, the .asc beside it, in a keyring of its own:
#   export GNUPGHOME=$(mktemp -d)
#   gpg --keyserver hkps://keys.openpgp.org --recv-keys <the key the .asc names>
#   gpg --verify libmpv-v<version>-x86_64-w64-mingw32-lgpl.zip.asc libmpv-v<version>-x86_64-w64-mingw32-lgpl.zip
# whose key has to be an mpv maintainer's: one listed on that maintainer's
# GitHub account (gh api users/<login>/gpg_keys), a member of mpv-player, and
# the one that signed the release's tag (git verify-tag in a clone of mpv).
# mpv names no single release key: 0.42.0's is Kacper Michajłow's,
# DE537FA4CD83E657227D6461D6CA75F6505F42A5, its signing subkey
# D83F25E44BD6B948724AB75F6580132338ABD4E2. Then change the URL and digest
# together, and the version THIRD-PARTY.md names.
WIN_LIBMPV_URL=https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/releases/download/v0.42.0/libmpv-v0.42.0-x86_64-w64-mingw32-lgpl.zip
WIN_LIBMPV_SHA256=8e5f77430efc53ef175804ba6618527e3af0448a0dcabf04d3cc72659d1a6fce

# The LGPLv3 text, as LICENSE-LGPLv3.txt beside libmpv-2.dll: the FFmpeg
# linked into it is configured as LGPL version 3 or later, which comes with
# the GPLv3's text (LICENSE-GPLv3.txt, there for yt-dlp) and its own. The
# zip carries only mpv's LGPL 2.1. FFmpeg's copy, from a tag; the text is the
# FSF's and doesn't change between tags.
WIN_LGPLV3_LICENSE_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/n9.0.2/COPYING.LGPLv3
WIN_LGPLV3_LICENSE_SHA256=da7eabb7bafdf7d3ae5e9f223aa5bdc1eece45ac569dc21b3b037520b4464768

# ffmpeg.exe, for the tests only: Gyan's "essentials" release build, which
# includes libx264 (the thumbnail test encodes with it). Gyan keeps release
# tags.
WIN_FFMPEG_URL=https://github.com/GyanD/codexffmpeg/releases/download/9.0.2/ffmpeg-9.0.2-essentials_build.7z
WIN_FFMPEG_SHA256=4705843ccaaf54257c16ad90f3e952ece33c17df964ecf7bfdbb0f49c7171077
